/E (US Formulations \(51% in Q1 FY25 vs 38% in FY22\): The company distributes over 200 generic products in the U.S. market, holding leadership positions in more than 20% of its product families and ranking among the top three in approximately 60% of its products. As the 5th largest generic company in the U.S., it has launched 67 new products between FY23 and Q1 FY25, including Indomethacin suppository and Zituvimet. By FY24, the company had secured 402 product approvals and 460 ANDA filings. Segment revenue grew by 49% from FY22 to FY24, driven by volume expansion and new product launches.)
